 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "induction hob keeps turnin off after 5-10 mins on high, have to keep restartin it. drives me nuts. any1 know y?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "This is likely caused by the hob’s built-in safety timer cutting power after a set duration or an overheating sensor triggering. You may need to check if a specific \"safety\" or \"child lock\" feature is active, as these often limit continuous high-heat usage. From what you have described, the most likely cause is the hob's cooling / ventilation. Is it a ceramic, solid-plate or induction hob, and does it trip the moment you switch it on, only when a certain zone is turned up, or after a spill/clean - with any burning smell?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "its induction. doesnt trip straight away, only after 5-10 mins on high, mostly the big front zones. no burning smell. fan goes loud before it cuts out"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Next: If a spill or clean preceded it, let the hob dry fully before assuming a failed part. Let me know what you find."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "no spill or clean b4 it, it just started after a new drawer unit was fitted under it a month ago. what should i do?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "You should contact the installer of the new drawer unit to check if they have obstructed the hob’s ventilation or caused damage, as this issue started after their work. Since the fan is making loud noises and cutting out under load, it likely indicates an internal fault that requires a qualified engineer to inspect safely. Could you tell me a bit more about what it is doing, and when it happens?"
  }
 ],
